---
import ContentLayout from '../../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import NewsletterSignup from '../../../components/NewsletterSignup.astro';
---
<ContentLayout title="Budget tech picks | StackGeist" description="Curated budget tech recommendations organized by price band and use case." active="gear">
  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / <a href="/gear/">Gear</a> / Budget tech</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">Budget tech</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Small upgrades that quietly fix annoying problems.</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">These catalog entries were migrated from an earlier editorial list. Each detail page now states its own evidence status: source-checked, owned-and-used where that record is explicitly supported, or research starting point when the technical evidence pass is incomplete.</p>

  <section class="owned-shortlist" data-owned-shortlist aria-labelledby="owned-shortlist-title">
    <div class="shortlist-head">
      <div><p class="page-kicker">Evidence-backed shortlist</p><h2 id="owned-shortlist-title">Start with pages that currently have the clearest evidence and decision context.</h2></div>
    </div>
    <div class="shortlist-grid">
      <article data-owned-pick><span>01 / video</span><h3><a href="/gear/budget-tech/logitech-c920x-hd-webcam/">Logitech C920x webcam</a></h3><p>Current first-party documentation supports the core connection, lens, microphone, and mounting facts used on the decision page.</p><a href="/guides/better-video-calls/">Check the full call setup →</a></article>
      <article data-owned-pick><span>02 / audio</span><h3><a href="/gear/budget-tech/sennheiser-momentum-4-wireless-noise-cancelling-headphones/">Sennheiser MOMENTUM 4</a></h3><p>Current Sennheiser documentation supports the codec, ANC, Bluetooth, multipoint, and published battery claims used on the decision page.</p><a href="/guides/sennheiser-momentum-4-wont-pair/">Pairing troubleshooting →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <form class="catalog-tools" role="search" data-catalog-tools>
    <label><span>find</span><input type="search" placeholder="webcam, cable, storage…" autocomplete="off" data-catalog-search /></label>
    <label><span>tier</span><select data-catalog-filter><option value="all">all sections</option><option value="under-25">under $25</option><option value="under-75">under $75</option><option value="essentials">everyday essentials</option><option value="premium">worth paying more</option></select></label>
    <label><span>research</span><select data-catalog-status><option value="all">all entries</option><option value="verified">source-checked detail</option><option value="editorial">editorial starting point</option></select></label>
    <output aria-live="polite" data-catalog-result>30 products</output>
  </form>
  <nav class="catalog-jumps" aria-label="Jump to product section"><span>jump:</span><a href="#under-25">under $25</a><a href="#under-75">under $75</a><a href="#essentials">essentials</a><a href="#premium">pay more</a></nav>

  <section class="content-section cards" id="compare">
    <a class="card" href="/gear/budget-tech/compare">
      <p class="page-kicker">Head to head</p>
      <h2>Compare before you buy</h2>
      <p>10 side-by-side comparisons that call the winner by user type. INIU vs generic USB-C, GaN station vs wall brick, Momentum 4 vs cheap ANC, and more.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">10 comparisons</span></div>
    </a>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section" id="under-25" data-catalog-section="under-25">
    <p class="page-kicker">Budget tier</p>
    <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/iniu-usb-c-to-usb-c-cable-240w-6-6ft">
      <h2>INIU USB-C to USB-C Cable (240W, 6.6ft)</h2>
      <p>Most USB-C cables are slow or inconsistent.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/140-in-1-precision-screwdriver-repair-kit">
      <h2>140-in-1 Precision Screwdriver Repair Kit</h2>
      <p>Electronics use annoying tiny screws, and the wrong tool will strip them instantly.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/flat-plug-surge-protector-power-strip-8-outlets-usb">
      <img class="product-thumb" src="/gear/flat-plug-surge-protector.jpg" alt="Flat Plug Surge Protector Power Strip (8 Outlets + USB)" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <h2>Flat Plug Surge Protector Power Strip (8 Outlets + USB)</h2>
      <p>Most power strips are cramped and useless once you plug in anything bulky.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/acodot-9-in-1-usb-c-hub">
      <h2>Acodot 9-in-1 USB-C Hub</h2>
      <p>Modern laptops keep removing ports.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/sabrent-sata-to-usb-adapter-cable">
      <h2>SABRENT SATA to USB Adapter Cable</h2>
      <p>If you’ve ever pulled a hard drive or SSD out of an old laptop, you know how annoying it is to access the data.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section" id="under-75" data-catalog-section="under-75">
    <p class="page-kicker">Mid-budget tier</p>
    <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/sandisk-ultra-128gb-microsd-card-2-pack">
      <h2>SanDisk Ultra 128GB microSD Card (2-Pack)</h2>
      <p>Cheap storage works until it doesn’t.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/500w-multi-port-gan-charging-station">
      <h2>500W Multi-Port GaN Charging Station</h2>
      <p>Charging setups get messy fast when every device needs its own brick.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/alfa-ac1900-long-range-usb-wi-fi-adapter">
      <h2>ALFA AC1900 Long-Range USB Wi-Fi Adapter</h2>
      <p>Built-in Wi-Fi adapters struggle in bad signal areas.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/sabrent-usb-c-lay-flat-drive-dock-nvme-sata">
      <h2>SABRENT USB-C Lay-Flat Drive Dock (NVMe + SATA)</h2>
      <p>Working with internal drives shouldn’t require a pile of adapters and screws.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/80w-soundbar-for-tv-pc-and-gaming">
      <h2>80W Soundbar for TV, PC, and Gaming</h2>
      <p>Built-in TV speakers are usually the weakest part of a setup.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="verified" href="/gear/budget-tech/logitech-c920x-hd-webcam">
      <h2>Logitech C920x HD Webcam</h2>
      <p>Built-in webcams are usually bad.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section" id="essentials" data-catalog-section="essentials">
    <p class="page-kicker">Everyday essentials</p>
    <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/sandisk-ultra-flair-128gb-usb-3-0-flash-drive">
      <h2>SanDisk Ultra Flair 128GB USB 3.0 Flash Drive</h2>
      <p>Small flash drives are easy to lose, but you still need one that actually holds a decent amount of data.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/15ft-indoor-extension-cord-16-3-flat-black">
      <h2>15ft Indoor Extension Cord (16/3, Flat Black)</h2>
      <p>Sometimes the outlet just isn’t where you need it.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/adjustable-desk-phone-stand">
      <h2>Adjustable Desk Phone Stand</h2>
      <p>Propping your phone against random objects gets old fast.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/adjustable-aluminum-tablet-stand">
      <h2>Adjustable Aluminum Tablet Stand</h2>
      <p>Holding a tablet for long periods gets uncomfortable fast.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/microfiber-cleaning-cloths-18-pack">
      <h2>Microfiber Cleaning Cloths (18-Pack)</h2>
      <p>Screens, glasses, and lenses get dirty constantly.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/usb-to-3-5mm-audio-adapter-cable">
      <h2>USB to 3.5mm Audio Adapter Cable</h2>
      <p>When a headphone jack stops working or doesn’t exist at all, audio gets annoying fast.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/clipboard-with-storage-compartment">
      <h2>Clipboard with Storage Compartment</h2>
      <p>Loose papers, notes, and small items get lost fast.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/80w-digital-soldering-iron-kit">
      <h2>80W Digital Soldering Iron Kit</h2>
      <p>This isn’t something everyone needs, but it’s cheap enough to be worth having if you do basic electronic repairs.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/usb-c-to-usb-a-adapter-2-pack">
      <h2>USB-C to USB-A Adapter (2-Pack)</h2>
      <p>A lot of older accessories still use USB-A, while newer devices are all USB-C.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/clamp-on-led-desk-lamp">
      <img class="product-thumb" src="/gear/clamp-on-led-desk-lamp.jpg" alt="Clamp-On LED Desk Lamp" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <h2>Clamp-On LED Desk Lamp</h2>
      <p>Bad lighting makes desk work harder than it needs to be.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section" id="premium" data-catalog-section="premium">
    <p class="page-kicker">Worth paying more for</p>
    <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/kroser-laptop-briefcase-up-to-17-3">
      <h2>KROSER Laptop Briefcase (Up to 17.3”)</h2>
      <p>Carrying a laptop in a flimsy bag is a good way to break expensive gear.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/samsung-evo-select-512gb-microsd-card">
      <img class="product-thumb" src="/gear/samsung-evo-select-512gb.jpg" alt="Samsung EVO Select 512GB microSD Card" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <h2>Samsung EVO Select 512GB microSD Card</h2>
      <p>Cheap microSD cards are fine until they corrupt or slow everything down.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/levo-g2-deluxe-rolling-laptop-stand">
      <h2>LEVO G2 Deluxe Rolling Laptop Stand</h2>
      <p>Working from a couch or bed usually means awkward angles and bad posture.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/canakit-raspberry-pi-5-starter-kit-pro-8gb-128gb">
      <h2>CanaKit Raspberry Pi 5 Starter Kit PRO (8GB, 128GB)</h2>
      <p>This isn’t a bare-bones Raspberry Pi setup.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="verified" href="/gear/budget-tech/sennheiser-momentum-4-wireless-noise-cancelling-headphones">
      <h2>Sennheiser Momentum 4 Wireless Noise-Cancelling Headphones</h2>
      <p>Noise is one of the fastest ways to lose focus.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/big-tall-high-back-office-chair-400lb-capacity">
      <img class="product-thumb" src="/gear/big-tall-office-chair.jpg" alt="Big & Tall High-Back Office Chair (400lb Capacity)" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <h2>Big & Tall High-Back Office Chair (400lb Capacity)</h2>
      <p>Cheap office chairs fail fast and punish your back even faster.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/14-portable-laptop-screen-extender-triple-display">
      <h2>14” Portable Laptop Screen Extender (Triple Display)</h2>
      <p>One laptop screen is a bottleneck.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/texas-instruments-ti-84-plus-ce-graphing-calculator">
      <h2>Texas Instruments TI-84 Plus CE Graphing Calculator</h2>
      <p>This is the calculator most schools and exams are built around.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    <a class="card" data-catalog-card data-status="editorial" href="/gear/budget-tech/wd-elements-portable-external-hard-drive">
      <h2>WD Elements Portable External Hard Drive</h2>
      <p>Running out of storage is inevitable if you keep files long enough.</p>
      <div class="card-meta"><span class="tag active">Budget tech</span></div>
    </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="note">Paid Amazon links are disclosed next to the retailer action and in the site footer. As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</div></section>
  <NewsletterSignup />
  <p class="catalog-empty" hidden data-catalog-empty>No products match that search. Try a broader problem or show all sections.</p>
  <style>
    .product-thumb { display:block; width:100%; height:200px; margin-bottom:16px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:0; object-fit:contain; background:#fff; }
    .owned-shortlist{margin-top:30px;border:1px solid var(--term-border);background:var(--term-bg)}.owned-shortlist::before{content:none;display:block;padding:10px 14px;border-bottom:1px dashed var(--term-border);color:var(--phosphor);font-size:.8rem}.shortlist-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;align-items:end;padding:22px}.shortlist-head h2{max-width:720px;margin:5px 0 0;font-size:clamp(20px,3vw,28px)}.shortlist-head>a,.shortlist-grid a{color:var(--purple-light);text-decoration:underline dotted;text-underline-offset:3px}.shortlist-head>a{flex-shrink:0;font-size:.8rem}.shortlist-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);border-top:1px solid var(--term-border)}.shortlist-grid article{padding:18px;border-left:1px solid var(--term-border)}.shortlist-grid article:first-child{border-left:0}.shortlist-grid span{color:var(--phosphor);font-size:.8rem}.shortlist-grid h3{margin:10px 0 8px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.35}.shortlist-grid p{min-height:82px;margin:0 0 14px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.55}.shortlist-grid article>a{font-size:.8rem}
    .catalog-tools{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(220px,1fr) 210px 240px auto;gap:10px;align-items:end;margin-top:28px;padding:16px;border:1px solid var(--term-border);background:var(--term-bg)}
    .catalog-tools label{display:grid;gap:7px;color:var(--phosphor);font-size:.8rem}.catalog-tools label span::before{content:none;margin-right:5px;color:var(--quiet)}
    .catalog-tools input,.catalog-tools select{width:100%;min-height:44px;padding:0 11px;border:1px solid var(--term-border-strong);border-radius:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:12px var(--font-sans)}
    .catalog-tools input:focus,.catalog-tools select:focus{outline:2px solid var(--purple-light);outline-offset:2px}.catalog-tools output{min-width:105px;padding-bottom:13px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;text-align:right}
    .catalog-jumps{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 14px;align-items:center;padding:12px 16px;border:1px solid var(--term-border);border-top:0;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.8rem}.catalog-jumps span{color:var(--phosphor)}.catalog-jumps a{display:inline-flex;min-height:32px;align-items:center;color:var(--purple-light);text-decoration:underline dotted;text-underline-offset:3px}
    [data-catalog-section][hidden]{display:none}.catalog-empty{margin:28px 0;padding:18px;border:1px solid var(--amber);color:var(--amber);font-size:.88rem}
    @media(max-width:1000px){.shortlist-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.shortlist-grid article{border-top:1px solid var(--term-border)}.shortlist-grid article:nth-child(odd){border-left:0}.shortlist-grid article:first-child,.shortlist-grid article:nth-child(2){border-top:0}}
    @media(max-width:900px){.catalog-tools{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.catalog-tools output{text-align:left;padding:4px 0}}
    @media(max-width:600px){.shortlist-head{display:grid}.shortlist-head>a{min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center}.shortlist-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.shortlist-grid article,.shortlist-grid article:nth-child(2){border-top:1px solid var(--term-border);border-left:0}.shortlist-grid article:first-child{border-top:0}.shortlist-grid p{min-height:0}.catalog-tools{grid-template-columns:1fr}.catalog-tools output{min-height:28px}.catalog-jumps a{min-height:44px}.product-thumb{height:220px}}
  </style>
  <script>
    const tools=document.querySelector('[data-catalog-tools]');
    const search=tools?.querySelector('[data-catalog-search]');
    const filter=tools?.querySelector('[data-catalog-filter]');
    const status=tools?.querySelector('[data-catalog-status]');
    const result=tools?.querySelector('[data-catalog-result]');
    const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-catalog-card]')];
    const sections=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-catalog-section]')];
    const empty=document.querySelector('[data-catalog-empty]');
    const update=()=>{const query=search?.value.trim().toLowerCase()||'';const tier=filter?.value||'all';const research=status?.value||'all';let shown=0;cards.forEach(card=>{const section=card.closest('[data-catalog-section]')?.getAttribute('data-catalog-section')||'compare';const matchesText=!query||card.textContent.toLowerCase().includes(query);const matchesTier=tier==='all'||tier===section;const matchesStatus=research==='all'||card.getAttribute('data-status')===research;const visible=matchesText&&matchesTier&&matchesStatus;card.hidden=!visible;if(visible)shown++;});sections.forEach(section=>{section.hidden=!section.querySelector('[data-catalog-card]:not([hidden])');});if(result)result.textContent=`${shown} result${shown===1?'':'s'}`;if(empty)empty.hidden=shown!==0;};
    search?.addEventListener('input',update);filter?.addEventListener('change',update);status?.addEventListener('change',update);update();
  </script>
</ContentLayout>
